WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.536
Our first guest tonight
is a Grammy-nominated musician

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.772
and actor whose new series,
"Unidentified with Demi Lovato,"

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.473
is streaming on September 30th
on Peacock.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:08.708
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.443
-You find something?

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.346
-Well, I don't totally know.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.481
-What?
-It's not moving.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:19.118
But it's bright like a star.
-But it's long.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.587
-That is actually very strange.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.722
-Yeah, do you see that?
-Isn't that weird?

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.457
More like a line than a dot.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.192
-The rest of them are all...
-Normal stars.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.926
-...perfectly round.
-Okay.

00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:32.132
So if the one with...

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:35.601
-Yeah, that's it.
You're dead on, Demi.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.737
-Please welcome back
to the show and the studio

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.572
our friend Demi Lovato.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.142
♪♪

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:45.344
-Hi.
-It's so good to see you.

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.847
Thanks for being here.
-Thank you.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.348
Hello.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.951
♪♪

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.420
-Welcome back. It's so nice to
have you here in person again.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.155
-Thank you.
It's so nice to be here.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.289
Thank you for having me.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:58.791
-Last time we talked,

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.359
I think it was in November
and you were telling me

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.627
that you were getting
into meditating.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.295
Have you continued to meditate,

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.464
as we are here
almost a year later?

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.800
-Yes.
I have stayed meditating.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.335
I meditated just this morning

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.672
and, you know,
yesterday morning,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.940
and it's been good.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.409
-Do you use an app?

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.977
I feel like a lot of people
are using apps now to meditate.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.879
-I do use an app sometimes.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.648
Sometimes, I use Insight Timer.
-Okay.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.784
-Which is really, really good
for, like, guided meditations.

00:01:25.784 --> 00:01:28.855
You can click, you know,
how long the meditation is

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.090
that you want to do,
and then just go from there.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.427
But other times, I just meditate
by myself and...

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.129
-How much time do you feel
like you need to give yourself

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:38.964
on any given day to meditate?

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:41.634
-I like to give myself --
You know, in the beginning,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.436
I was really, really into it,

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.305
and I was giving myself
like 30 minutes.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.972
Then that turned into
like an hour,

00:01:46.972 --> 00:01:48.875
then it turned into
an hour and a half.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.144
And now it's back down
to like 10 minutes.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.012
[ Laughs ]
It didn't stay that...

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.781
-Well, you're very busy.
-Yes.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.415
-I would find it hard to believe

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.383
that you had 90 minutes
every day to meditate.

00:01:58.383 --> 00:01:59.586
-I did in quarantine.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.120
-Okay, right.
That's a good point, yes.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.222
-And now I'm not in quarantine.
-You're back in the world,

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.091
and we're very happy
to have you back in the world

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.360
because we have
this wonderful show now.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.230
The subject matter of this show
comes as no surprise to me.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.498
The first time we met
was back in 2014,

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.867
the first year of this show.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.601
-Yes.
-You came in.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.403
We talked a lot about
how you were a believer

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.372
in the extraterrestrial,

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.575
the world of ghosts, mermaids.
-Yes.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.577
-Which I -- This was stuff
that I didn't know about you.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.045
I was delighted to hear.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.682
And how -- So what do you
set out to do in the show?

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.517
-So, what I'm trying
to set out to do in the show

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:35.388
is just to gather evidence,
gather information

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:39.292
and try to make the best --

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.628
best guess of what
it might be that's out there.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.598
-Part of this, of course,
must be the fun of the journey

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.868
because these are gonna be
really hard answers to find.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.336
You're doing it with people

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.338
you obviously get along with
and love very much.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.007
That's one of the joys
of the show.

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:57.009
Talk about who you are
doing this with.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.244
-I am doing this
with my best friend,

00:02:59.244 --> 00:03:01.147
Matthew Scott Montgomery,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.716
and my older sister,
Dallas Lovato.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:07.353
And it was just so much fun to
shoot with them because they --

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.657
Well, first, Matthew and I
always have a blast together.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.191
And then, second, it was really,

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.861
really great to spend time
with my older sister

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.829
because you know
when you get older,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.998
you just don't get to spend
as much time

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.933
around your family members
as you once did.

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.635
-Of course.
-And so it's really,

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.638
really nice to be able
to build our relationship

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.875
and have fun together doing
stuff that we all really enjoy.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.777
-So you're obviously
the believer of the group.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.613
Are either of them the skeptic?
Do you have a skeptic?

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:37.483
-They are more skeptical
than I am.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.718
And I would say
the skeptic of the group

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:41.454
would have to be Matthew.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.656
Matthew is very, very skeptical.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.925
I mean, he was basically you.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:48.994
[ Laughs ]
He was you out there.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.362
-I'm glad.

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.064
I want to make sure that
I'm represented on this show,

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:53.198
even though
I'm very happy to say

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:55.134
I get to make a little cameo
in the show.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.769
-Yes.
-I appear via Zoom

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.404
and got to talk to you about

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.972
some of the stuff
you're discovering.

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:02.675
And one of the cool things
is you are talking to people

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.910
who believe they've had these

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.347
extraterrestrial interactions,
scientists.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:10.516
How do you put together
this list of the people

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.318
that you want
to talk to for the show?

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.688
-Well, the list actually came
from some of the producers.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:20.626
The producers had worked
on various projects

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.595
that were UFO and ET-related,

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.763
so they had
all of the connections.

00:04:24.763 --> 00:04:27.733
And all I did basically was
just go along for the ride.

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:29.902
And I was like a kid
in a candy shop.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.739
I was so excited
to meet these people

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:38.277
who had had these
firsthand experiences and --

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:41.047
Wow. Did they have a lot to say.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.582
-So you went
to a support group.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:45.684
Is that -- Am I using
the terminology right?

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:47.085
Of people who, you know,

00:04:47.085 --> 00:04:49.655
believe that they've sort of
had these moments?

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.056
-Yes.
-And when you went,

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:53.426
what did they sort of tell you
when you go into the room?

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:56.061
Did they want you to ask
a lot of questions or...?

00:04:56.061 --> 00:05:01.100
-I basically went and just
listened for most of it.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.803
It felt like a --

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:07.873
It felt like a support group
that, you know --

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:10.542
but for people
who have had experiences

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.178
with ETs, UFOs.

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:18.885
And when I first went in there,
I was just, like, in awe

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.686
at some of the things
that I was hearing,

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.556
and it also didn't
make me feel so alone.

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.392
Because there's a lot of times
when I tell people

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.994
that I believe in this stuff,
they look at me like

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:32.865
I've lost my marbles,
and that's okay.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.634
But, yeah.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.970
It was cool to talk to a bunch
of people that also believe

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.606
in some of the things
that I do and realize,

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.608
oh, we're kind of all
in this together.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.044
-Are you worried that
by doing a show like this,

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:50.115
it will make ETs less likely
to interact with you in the fear

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:52.451
that they might get
caught on camera?

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:54.553
Like, I feel like each
of these interviews we do,

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.388
that if an ET is watching it,
they'd be like,

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:58.624
"Well, Seth's the one
we should [bleep] with

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:03.196
because, like,
he's the one who deserves it."

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.497
But they'll just stay
clear of you.

00:06:05.497 --> 00:06:08.634
-Well, I've come to learn
that the way

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:12.871
to make these interactions
with these beings

00:06:12.871 --> 00:06:15.307
are by expanding
our consciousness.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:16.876
So, through meditation,

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:20.145
we actually can make contact
a lot easier,

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:23.482
and it's been so many times
where I've been meditating,

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.884
and I've looked up, and
there's something in the sky.

00:06:25.884 --> 00:06:27.720
And so I think that
through meditation,

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.055
you can make it happen yourself.

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:31.323
-You also did --
You went under hypnosis

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:33.625
to see if you had
any sort of past experiences.

00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:34.994
-Yes.
-Why did they discover?

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.530
Or what did you discover,
I should say, when you did that?

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.532
-Well, I would tell you, but
you have to watch to find out.

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:42.535
-All right. That's very fair.
-You know?

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:43.870
Because if I give it away...

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.237
-Hey, look,
I'm in the TV business.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:46.972
I have a lot of respect
for what you just did.

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:48.574
-Okay, thank you.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:51.077
-What about --
You also have a podcast now.

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.945
-Yes.

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.747
-And this is not unique

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:57.750
to just extraterrestrial stuff,
or is it?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.954
-Right. No, it is not
just for UFOs and ETs.

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:06.659
It is -- I talk about
a plethora of topics.

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:11.663
I talk to friends of mine
that are in the industry,

00:07:11.663 --> 00:07:13.833
people that aren't
in the industry,

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:17.636
people that are scientists,

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:21.040
just people that know a lot
about a lot of stuff,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.242
and I am just interested in
learning what they have to say.

00:07:24.242 --> 00:07:26.745
-You've always struck me
as very thoughtful and curious.

00:07:26.745 --> 00:07:29.048
Do you like being someone
who asks the questions

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:31.650
as opposed
to getting them asked?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.819
-I do, I really do,
because I love learning.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:35.921
And I feel like I get to learn
so much more

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:38.290
by listening than I do talking.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.592
[ Laughter ]
-That's why I just like to talk.

00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:42.627
-[ Laughs ] Got it.
-I feel like I know

00:07:42.627 --> 00:07:44.163
everything I want to know.
-Got it.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.298
-Hey, it's always such
a pleasure to have you here.

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:48.400
-It's such a pleasure.
-Thanks for making the time.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.369
"Unidentified with Demi Lovato"
is available to stream

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:53.906
on Peacock on September 30th.
That is technically right now.

